## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to extend Dijkstra's algorithm to count shortest paths while handling ties and modular arithmetic—a common pattern in competitive programming and graph algorithms.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm with path counting augmentation
- Non-negative edge weights, including zero-weight edges
- Modular arithmetic for large path counts and overflow prevention
- Edge case handling: unreachable destinations, multiple optimal paths, zero-weight cycles

## Code Example
```javascript
function countShortestPaths(n, edges, s, t) {
  const MOD = 1e9 + 7;
  const dist = new Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const ways = new Array(n).fill(0);

  dist[s] = 0;
  ways[s] = 1;

  const pq = new MinPriorityQueue({ priority: x => dist[x] });
  pq.enqueue(s);

  while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
    const u = pq.dequeue().element;

    for (const [v, w] of edges[u]) {
      if (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + w;
        ways[v] = ways[u];
        pq.enqueue(v);
      } else if (dist[u] + w === dist[v]) {
        ways[v] = (ways[v] + ways[u]) % MOD;
      }
    }
  }

  return { distance: dist[t] === Infinity ? -1 : dist[t], paths: ways[t] };
}
```

## Time & Space Complexity
- **Time**: O((N + M) log N) due to priority queue operations
- **Space**: O(N) for distance and path count arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Tests per-key streaming stats with independent sliding windows, combining deques, hashtables, and a heap with lazy expirations. It mirrors real services that analyze per-entity signals under time constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key deques for time-bounded data
- Hash map for key -> stats
- Max-heap with lazy deletion to keep top averages up-to-date
- Expiration handling driven by currentTime

## Code Example
```javascript
class PerKeyRollingStats {
  constructor(W) { this.W = W; this.map = new Map(); this.heap = new MaxHeap(); }
  add(key, value, ts) {
    let rec = this.map.get(key) || { dq: [], sum: 0 };
    rec.dq.push([ts, value]);
    rec.sum += value;
    while (rec.dq.length && rec.dq[0][0] < ts - this.W) {
      const [t, v] = rec.dq.shift();
      rec.sum -= v;
    }
    this.map.set(key, rec);
    const avg = rec.sum / rec.dq.length;
    this.heap.push({ key, avg, validAt: ts, len: rec.dq.length });
  }
  topK(currentTime, K) {
    const res = [];
    while (res.length < K) {
      const top = this.heap.pop();
      if (!top) break;
      const rec = this.map.get(top.key);
      const avg = rec && rec.dq.length ? rec.sum / rec.dq.length : -Infinity;
      if (top.avg !== avg) continue; // stale entry
      res.push(top.key);
    }
    // optional: reinsert from a temp to preserve heap state
    return res;
  }
}
```

